  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Cedar Hills Rotary Park is a tight, wooded, hilly course of championship caliber that winds through a scenic underdeveloped city park in Raleigh. From the red tees it plays 4,907 feet at par 54, with blue and yellow layouts adding distance and a couple of par 4s for the advanced crowd.",
    "Free to play with mixed tees and DISCatcher baskets, it's the course where Raleigh's woods players sharpen their lines. The hills make the walks honest and the shots interesting — every fairway is a corridor, every green is guarded.",
    "It's older than the internet (1984) and still one of the most respected technical tests in the Triangle."
  ],
