  "layoutMapUrl": null,
  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 18 closes Cedar Hills at 380 feet — the longest hole on the card and the perfect final exam for a course built on tight lines and honest hills. From the tee you're threading the woods; from the landing zone you're attacking a green that the terrain defends. It's the hole that makes a clean round here feel earned.",
  "localTips": "The red tees are the standard loop; blue and yellow add distance and turn holes 13 and 18 into par 4s. Free to play but genuinely technical — the hills and woods don't let up. Wear grippy shoes and bring your accuracy game.",
